{"id": "EUVD-2026-76449", "enisaUuid": "19de081b-0969-39bd-a200-d79cb2b88f29", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nSUNRPC: Reject krb5 v2 wrap tokens with oversized ec field\n\ngss_krb5_unwrap_v2() sets buf->len to a logical\nlength, which can be much smaller than head[0].iov_len\n(the allocated receive-page capacity).  It then calls\nxdr_buf_trim() with a trim length derived from the 16-bit\n\"extra count\" (ec) field in the Kerberos v2 token header.\n\nThe ec field is authenticated by the post-decrypt memcmp()\nagainst the encrypted header copy, so a randomly-mutated\nvalue is rejected.  However, any peer holding a valid GSS\ncontext can legitimately encrypt a token whose ec exceeds\nthe plaintext length.  Per RFC 4121, such a token is\nstructurally malformed.\n\nAlthough xdr_buf_trim() now clamps the buf->len subtraction\nto avoid unsigned underflow, the buffer is still left in a\nsemantically invalid state (zero length, inconsistent iov\nlengths) when ec is oversized.\n\nReject these tokens before calling xdr_buf_trim(), giving\ncallers a well-defined GSS_S_DEFECTIVE_TOKEN error and\nkeeping the xdr_buf internally consistent.  The wrapped blob\nbegins at a nonzero offset -- both callers pass len as\noffset + opaque_len -- so buf->len still counts the offset\nbytes that precede the blob.  Compare the trim length\nagainst the remaining wrapped segment, buf->len - offset,\nrather than the whole buffer; comparing against buf->len\nalone leaves an offset-wide window in which an oversized ec\npasses the test and xdr_buf_trim() cuts into the bytes ahead\nof the blob.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:48:29", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac9efc29346b6942e71f0e24a3178a9121330fab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5746095b59f4d11f39f08751d36bbdfd1e5deac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9fc6d6e6db49ab55208d5dd1c424c1d0d9aa7296", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4abb44a29bb515df6f49123848765c70fc9b5021", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dfcd81ab45613d45996fbf483d4ef54b0ec90ab9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1f9856af065b6158271687e9788407b9573fd16f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/880effc943ed82d6811f272ed3307c222b40f4d6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad484748eec0a66eac0f13ab53b3fbedb7333c91"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89538", "GHSA-3r47-q2hr-fjxp"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.71, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2338e4fe-ea13-3a21-a89f-ec75a49a12cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cf4c024b908353fcc48309374d39e3399d67dfd1 <880effc943ed82d6811f272ed3307c222b40f4d6"}, {"id": "27334b6a-3187-37e2-b7c4-e44f87501876", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2c787416-bbe5-32fc-8918-7da7bf16dab5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cf4c024b908353fcc48309374d39e3399d67dfd1 <4abb44a29bb515df6f49123848765c70fc9b5021"}, {"id": "362d62ab-83b4-3d03-b1b1-3be5737d0e37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cf4c024b908353fcc48309374d39e3399d67dfd1 <ad484748eec0a66eac0f13ab53b3fbedb7333c91"}, {"id": "37b04d7a-ee0e-3f6b-aef4-6128ba23b26f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cf4c024b908353fcc48309374d39e3399d67dfd1 <1f9856af065b6158271687e9788407b9573fd16f"}, {"id": "51824db5-86cf-3bcb-9a02-f92b01abfcbd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.13"}, {"id": "61de3d69-b0d3-39fb-8d18-fc4c8d97f65a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "6d7bb82c-f3d4-3dde-8af2-d0500b0dbc47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7557a6c4-f63b-351f-a4